  "coverage": [
    {
      "id": "NFR1",
      "status": "N/A",
      "target": "Not applicable to this unit. NFR1 is the Performance group (response time, throughput, resource ceiling). u2-domain-vocabulary is a leaf library with no runtime process, no request handling, no I/O and no measured latency surface; every value it exposes is a frozen constant or a pure function over in-memory data, so there is no request path whose response time this unit could contribute to. The measured surfaces NFR1 binds on - the asset list query, the dashboard aggregation and the CSV export - belong to u3-write-path, u4-reporting and u5-presentation, where they are adjudicated against the shared counting definition this unit owns."
    },
    {
      "id": "NFR2",
      "status": "OK",
      "target": "NFR2.1.1, NFR2.1.2, NFR2.1.3, NFR2.1.4, NFR2.1.5, NFR2.1.6, NFR2.1.7, NFR2.2.1, NFR2.2.2, NFR2.4.1, NFR2.5.1, NFR2.7.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "NFR3",
      "status": "OK",
      "target": "NFR3.2.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "NFR4",
      "status": "N/A",
      "target": "Not applicable to this unit. NFR4 is the Accessibility group (WCAG conformance, keyboard navigation, focus visibility, screen-reader semantics). u2-domain-vocabulary renders nothing, emits no markup, produces no stylesheet token and serves no route; its exports are JavaScript values consumed by the presentation unit. The rendered-surface accessibility requirements are adjudicated in the functional-design deliverables of u5-presentation."
    },
    {
      "id": "NFR5",
      "status": "N/A",
      "target": "Not applicable to this unit. NFR5 is the Scalability group (single-process topology, aggregate counting without loading the full asset set, medium-scale asset-list behaviour). u2-domain-vocabulary holds no process, no database handle and no list renderer; NFR5.1 binds the release deployment shape under constraint C4, NFR5.2 binds the counting path in u4-reporting, and NFR5.3 binds the asset-list surface in u5-presentation. This unit owns the shared counting definition those units consume, but it performs no count and scales no load of its own."
    },
    {
      "id": "NFR6",
      "status": "OK",
      "target": "NFR6.1.1, NFR6.3.1, NFR6.6.1"
    }
  ],
